{
  "id": "product-liability",
  "name": "Product Liability",
  "description": "Product liability claim for a personal injury. Written for counsel for Defendant, who must advise whether to litigate or to pay a settlement demand of $500,000.\n\nPlaintiff claims that she was injured by Defendant's product, and seeks compensatory damages. Punitive damages are not at issue.\n\n## Liability\n\n**State-of-the-art defense.** Defendant wants to argue to the jury that it is not liable because its product was safe on the risks that were known at the time it was sold. The judge must first decide whether to allow this defense. Counsel estimates a 60% chance that the judge does not allow it, and a 40% chance that the judge does.\n\nIf the defense is allowed, the jury decides whether the product was safe on the risks known at the time of sale. If it finds that the product was safe, Defendant is not liable, even if the product caused the injury. The answer depends heavily on whether the jury hears evidence of the current FDA standard, which is stringent. Counsel estimates a 25% chance that the current FDA standard is admissible. If it is, there is a 90% chance that the jury finds that the product was not safe. If it is not, the chance is 50%.\n\n**Causation.** Unless the state-of-the-art defense succeeds, Defendant is liable if the jury finds that its product caused Plaintiff's injury. That depends heavily on a Daubert motion by Defendant to exclude one of Plaintiff's doctors from testifying. Counsel estimates two chances in three that the judge denies the motion, and one chance in three that the judge grants it. If the motion is denied and the doctor testifies, there is an 80% chance that the jury finds that the product caused the injury. If the motion is granted, the chance is 40%.\n\n## Damages\n\nThe doctor's testimony also affects the award. If the motion is denied and Defendant is liable, counsel estimates a 25% chance of an award of about $1,000,000, a 50% chance of about $500,000, and a 25% chance of about $200,000. If the motion is granted and Defendant is liable, a 25% chance of about $800,000, a 50% chance of about $400,000, and a 25% chance of about $200,000.\n\nThe costs of litigation are left out.",
